course: dictionary
lesson: 5593
title: Words that name a permission
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «Only chefs with a special licence may prepare fugu» tells you a licence is an official permission to do a job. The clue is the word may: the licence gives permission.
explain: «A speed camera photographs cars going over the limit, and the driver must pay a fine and may get points on their licence.» Here a licence is a card a driver carries, and points are written on it. The words around it show you which meaning fits.
explain: In «poetic licence», licence means freedom: a writer may change facts or rules for effect. Ask yourself: is this a paper, or is it a freedom? Put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A licence is an official paper or card that gives you permission to do or own something.
fact: Examples of licences are a driving licence, a fishing licence and a TV licence.
fact: Licence can also mean freedom to do or say what you like, as in «poetic licence».
fact: In American English the noun is spelled license, and a licence plate is called a license plate.
exercise: «Only chefs with a special licence may prepare fugu.» What is a licence here? | A kind of poison | A type of fish | *An official permission to do a job | A bowl for cooking
exercise: In «poetic licence», what does licence mean? | A fee paid to a zoo | *Freedom to change facts or rules for effect | A kind of poem | A card that proves you can drive
exercise: Find and copy one word from «the driver must pay a fine and may get points on their licence» that means money paid as a punishment. | photographs | *fine | limit | driver
test: «Trained bat workers need a licence to open a bat box.» What is a licence in this sentence? | A box for bats | A kind of bat | *An official permission
test: «Every zoo needs a licence and regular inspections.» What does this tell you about a zoo licence? | *It is official permission to run a zoo, and it can be taken away | It is a kind of animal food | It is a free ticket for visitors
exam: Which sentence uses licence to mean freedom rather than an official paper? | *«Poetic licence» means a writer may change facts for effect | Only chefs with a special licence may prepare fugu | The driver must pay a fine and may get points on their licence | Every zoo needs a licence and regular inspections
